---
const letters=Array.from({length:7},(_,row)=>Array.from({length:5},(_,col)=>({row,col}))).flat().filter(({row,col})=>col===0||col===4||row===3);
---
<section class="guitar-learning" data-salience-selection aria-label="Salience and posterior parietal stimulation">
  <div class="salience-choices">
    <label>Stimulus bias<select data-salience-bias><option value="global">Global stands out</option><option value="local">Local stands out</option></select></label>
    <label>Task instruction<select data-salience-target><option value="global">Name the global letter</option><option value="local">Name the local letter</option></select></label>
    <label>Comparison condition<select data-salience-condition><option value="pre">Pre-TMS</option><option value="left">Left PPC TMS</option><option value="right">Right PPC TMS</option></select></label>
  </div>
  <div class="learning-screen">
    <svg class="learning-circuit salience-diagram" viewBox="0 0 1280 620" role="img" aria-labelledby="salience-title salience-desc">
      <title id="salience-title">Selecting more or less salient information</title><desc id="salience-desc">A large H is made from small S letters. Stimulus bias determines which level stands out; the task determines which level to name. Compare the reported effect of left or right posterior parietal TMS with pre-TMS performance.</desc>
      <text x="48" y="32" class="diagram-eyebrow">SALIENCE-BASED SELECTION</text><text x="48" y="76" class="diagram-heading">Which level stands out?</text><text x="48" y="112" class="diagram-note">Global / local describes scale. More / less salient describes what stands out.</text>
      <rect x="48" y="148" width="480" height="420" fill="#f4f0e5" stroke="#c5cec1"/>
      <g data-salience-letters class="global-bias">{letters.map(({row,col},i)=><text x={140+col*73} y={209+row*51} class:list={['local-letter',i%2===0?'alternate-a':'alternate-b']}>S</text>)}</g>
      <text x="576" y="181" class="salience-key">TASK</text><text x="576" y="222" class="salience-value" data-salience-task>Name the global letter: H</text>
      <text x="576" y="281" class="salience-key">TARGET SALIENCE</text><text x="576" y="322" class="salience-value" data-salience-level>More salient</text>
      <text x="576" y="381" class="salience-key">COMPARISON</text><text x="576" y="422" class="salience-value" data-salience-comparison>Pre-TMS reference</text>
      <rect x="565" y="455" width="660" height="110" rx="4" fill="#edf0e9" stroke="#b5c3ad"/><text x="586" y="493" class="salience-key">REPORTED RESULT</text><text x="586" y="534" class="salience-result" data-salience-result>Reveal after setting the comparison</text>
      <text x="48" y="603" class="diagram-note">PPC = posterior parietal cortex · TMS temporarily interferes with regional function.</text>
    </svg>
    <div class="learning-caption" aria-live="polite"><span data-salience-stage>SETUP</span><p data-salience-caption>Blurring the small S letters favors the global H. The instruction determines which level to select.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="learning-controls"><button type="button" data-salience-reveal>Reveal study result</button><button type="button" data-salience-reset>↺ Reset</button><button type="button" data-illustration-fullscreen>⛶ Fullscreen</button></div>
  <p class="learning-limit">Twelve finite study conditions. Results are qualitative comparisons from this task, not measured performance of the viewer.</p>
</section>
<style>
  .salience-choices{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:0 0 18px}.salience-choices label{font-size:12px;color:#a9c2cc;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px}.salience-choices select{background:#102735;color:#eafaff;border:1px solid #365563;border-radius:3px;padding:8px;max-width:100%}.local-letter{font-size:43px;font-weight:600;fill:#1d3552;text-anchor:middle}.global-bias{filter:blur(2px)}.local-bias .alternate-a{fill:#bd4b96}.local-bias .alternate-b{fill:#2d718f}.salience-key{font-size:17px;font-weight:600;fill:#536373;letter-spacing:.8px}.salience-value{font-size:29px;font-weight:600;fill:#1d3552}.salience-result{font-size:23px;fill:#1d3552}
</style>
